Pipkin Sprocketwhistle, a gnome warlock with a perpetually worried expression, adjusted his spectacles and glared at the dense foliage of Stranglethorn Vale. “Honestly, Beatrice,” he muttered to his succubus, who was currently attempting to seduce a particularly grumpy-looking boar, “this is *not* efficient. We’re supposed to be gathering moonpetal blossoms for Old Man Fitzwilliam’s potion!”

Beatrice, predictably, ignored him, batting her eyelashes at the boar and occasionally unleashing a distracting “Seduction” spell. Pipkin sighed, activating his own “Lash of Pain” – a surprisingly effective tactic against the stubborn beast. He’d chosen Beatrice for leveling, mostly because she was… entertaining. And, let’s be honest, her threat generation was superior to his Voidwalker’s. 

Suddenly, a large, snarling raptor charged. Pipkin instinctively channeled “Sacrifice,” erecting a shimmering shield just as Beatrice, abandoning her romantic pursuits, unleashed a flurry of “Lashes of Pain.” They survived, covered in mud and boar slobber, but with a full pouch of moonpetal blossoms. “Right,” Pipkin declared, “let’s get this over with.”



**Answer:** Voidwalkers are preferred for tanking due to their superior threat generation and defensive cooldowns (Torment, Sacrifice), making them better suited for sustained combat encounters, while succubuses excel at single-target damage and stealth, which is less crucial for the majority of leveling and questing. [end of text]


